    {
      "text": "Diagrama de clases UML del perfil Security. Vulnerability (publishedTime, modifiedTime, withdrawnTime) especializa Core/Artifact. La clase abstracta VulnAssessmentRelationship especializa Core/Relationship, restringe «to» a exactamente un Element y añade assessedElement, suppliedBy y las tres fechas; la especializan CvssV2/V3/V4VulnAssessmentRelationship (score, severity, vectorString), EpssVulnAssessmentRelationship (probability, percentile), ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship (catalogType, exploited, locator), SsvcVulnAssessmentRelationship (decisionType) y la clase abstracta VexVulnAssessmentRelationship (vexVersion, statusNotes). La clase VEX tiene cuatro subclases: VexAffected (actionStatement[1], actionStatementTime), VexFixed, VexNotAffected (justificationType, impactStatement, impactStatementTime) y VexUnderInvestigation. Enumeraciones: CvssSeverityType, ExploitCatalogType, SsvcDecisionType, VexJustificationType.",
